AC97  codecs contain the analog‐to‐digital (A/D), digital‐to‐ana‐
log (D/A), and mixing circuitry of many modern sound cards.  AC97
codecs, for the most part, do not talk to host  busses  like  the
PCI bus directly.  Instead, they communicate through an interface
chip,  called  the host controller.  The Ensoniq AudioPCI 97 (see
is an example of such a host controller.   Unlike  many  drivers,
the  driver  does not appear in the configuration file.  Instead,
the driver is automatically attached by the drivers that  require
it.   The driver does not keep track of the current user settings
and instead relies on the hardware to do this.  The driver  could
do  more  to  detect mixer channels that don’t work and cull them
from the list.
